      "tool": "Saved build GDB 15.1 command output/report and existing r4 syscall/r5 futex analysis; no new capture."
    },
    "fix_path": "**Owner:** BUILD through `build/build-management`, after the revision-6 investigation-review cross-stage approval. No capture is authorized before that approval.\n\nAfter r6 cross-stage approval, run one 600-frame diagnostic on the same assigned camera using the fixed FFmpeg executable and unchanged default production argv. Keep the 1280\u00d7720 MJPEG-to-NV12 mode, one decoder thread, one filter thread, queue size 1, and the same camera and reader fixed. Save no frame payload. After startup, arm a one-shot monotonic watchdog for each in-flight full-frame read; if that read remains incomplete beyond 60 ms, trigger at most one snapshot for it. Do not re-arm until that full frame completes, and cap the run at three snapshots total. Verify the target PID is the live FFmpeg child launched by the controller and that its `/proc/<pid>/exe` and command line match the fixed executable and expected argv. For each trigger, record monotonic trigger, attach, detach, and full-read-completion times plus debugger pause duration. Use the bounded batch invocation `gdb --quiet --batch --nx --pid <pid> -ex 'set pagination off' -ex 'set confirm off' -ex 'set debuginfod enabled off' -ex 'info threads' -ex 'thread apply all bt 16' -ex 'detach' -ex 'quit'`; retain its TID/LWP mapping and stacks. Do not use strace or another tracer. Abort and clean up if PID verification, attach, backtrace collection, or detach fails.\n\nGDB stops FFmpeg threads while collecting each snapshot, so these pauses perturb cadence and may extend the triggering read gap. The snapshots are for callsite localization only; their timings cannot measure AC-4 and do not establish causality. Keep the timestamp contract unchanged: `timestampEof` remains host-monotonic at complete raw-frame read, and source PTS remain SOE. A separate accepted five-minute AC-4 run remains the acceptance measure after any future approved product change.",
    "mechanism": "**Medium confidence:** cadence jitter remains after V4L2 buffer dequeue and inside FFmpeg processing/output before raw-pipe delivery. Futex waits correlate with long gaps, and the output-writer wait intervals have temporal same-address positive wake calls from the FFmpeg leader. This does not identify the awakened waiter or prove that a wake caused a gap. The GDB feasibility check established non-elevated attachment only to a disposable same-UID Python process; it adds no FFmpeg stack or callsite evidence. Reader-side backlog, primary CPU runqueue delay, sustained pipe backpressure, and a repeatable `-flush_packets 1` effect remain unsupported. The exact FFmpeg wait/processing cause remains unresolved.",
